From 188bfbea7cf2ccdd5b9caf102defb4fee09affb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominggoes Isakh <drjisakh@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:14:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/17] Update API lint baseline for restored camera2.legacy
 classes

The camera HALv1 restoration reintroduces android.hardware.camera2.legacy
classes that predate several current API lint requirements
(@FlaggedApi on new API, nullability annotations, array-vs-Collection
parameter style, acronym casing). These are internal legacy
compatibility shims, not new public API, so baseline them the same way
the build's own error message instructs rather than annotating 600+
pre-existing methods.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I507274980f6a26526210dd2b54fa1da614f84cd4
---
